0 -1 21007 0
E
oil painting picture fury blight nameless daemon decoration~
Upon closer inspection you realize what this painting is depicting.  You
shiver as you remember the tale, as it was told to you by the old man back at
the ol' Tickler...

"It was those three Scion heroes who came up with the idea.  It was pretty
much a fairly normal night up to that point...we had just started the drinking
for the evening, when Blight, Fury, and Nameless began discussing what lay
beyond the horrible gate, deep in the ghoul kingdom.  Not since Drazuk himself
was a mortal had anyone tried to enter the prison of the Elder Gods."

"Defeating the Gate Guardian to gain entrance was only the first step.  Soon
after entering, they realized there was no going back, not without cutting
that astral thread even shorter...so they marched on together, slaying the
evil spawn of chaos that swarmed them from all sides.  That dark experimenter
Nyarlathotep gave them pause, but the Three swept him aside."

"On the approach to Dagon, Dark Master of the Seas, disaster struck.  Mi-gos
and Deep Ones came from nowhere and brought the mighty Fury down.  Undaunted,
the heroes regrouped and moved forward once again.  Cutting through the
imprisoned gods, they finally approached the Black Pentagram that kept
Azathoth, Daemon-Sultan, imprisoned."

"Ready for their foe, they battered him until he fell with a mighty roar.
Exhausted, yet empowered with the excitement of victory, the Three gathered
around to congratulate each other.  Much to their dismay, over the panting of
their breath, they heard a gruff breathing behind them....they turned to see
that by some trick of time and fate, Azathoth had been reborn, and they were
still standing in the middle of his Pentagram, fully under his powers!"

"Nameless turned and whipped wicked kicks into the daemons face, and Blight
and Fury hammered him with equally powerful blows, while hastily calling upon
their Goddess for symbols of her power, many of which were burned calling the
healing power of Ashlyn down upon the stout warrior-monk.  Nameless began to
sag under the magical onslaught of the huge beast before him, but the strength
of the Three once again brought down their enemy."

"Not wishing to fight the creature anytime soon (bad enough that apparently
some of their belongings were left behind), they quickly moved out of the
pentagram, and stepped into a magical world...only that's where they stopped
their tale, and only grinned and saluted each other with another mug of ale."

~
S
#21007
The Temple Of Drazuk -- Donation Room~
This portion of the temple houses a large pit, used for storing items donated
by other adventurers.  It's worth a look to see if there is anything helpful
located within.
